<title>SWEDEN: Investor net asset value up 58 pct '96.</title>
<headline>Investor net asset value up 58 pct '96.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish investment company Investor AB, the key holding company in the Wallenberg family's financial empire, posted 1996 earnings on Thursday.</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>							1996	  1995</p>
<p> Net asset value on Dec 31		  78,880 vs  50,074</p>
<p>( Feb 17 -  85,168)</p>
<p> Net asset value/share on Dec 31 (SKR)     394 vs     252</p>
<p>(Feb 17 - 426 SKR)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit				  9,598 vs   3,048</p>
<p> Proposed dividend  (SKR)		    10.00 vs    9.00</p>
<p> Dividend income on main holdings	  1,804 vs     656</p>
<p> Capital gain, Scania			 12,400 vs	 0</p>
<p> Capital expense Saab Auto		   2,481 vs	 0</p>
<p> Other operating income		     13,963 vs  14,121</p>
<p> Other operating costs			13,846 vs  13,110</p>
<p> Group administrative costs		    444 vs     322</p>
<p> Depreciation				    1,830 vs   1,127</p>
<p> Operating profit				9,566 vs     218</p>
<p> Net financial items		     CREDIT 32 vs     450CHARGE</p>
<p> Taxes						 105 vs	64</p>
<p> Minority interests				 14 vs	 8</p>
<p> Net profit					9,479 vs   2,976</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
